'''FC Avanhard Zhovti Vody''' is a [[Ukraine|Ukrainian]] amateur football club from [[Zhovti Vody]], [[Dnipropetrovsk Oblast]].

In 1959–70 as Avanhard the club participated in the championship of the [[Ukrainian SSR]] among teams of masters (professional). Since 1993 it was known as Sirius and in 1994 moved to [[Kryvyi Rih]]. In 1995 Sirius was merged with a local amateur team Sportinvest Kryvyi Rih which replaced Sirius in competition for year. In 1996 the club folded. It was replaced by [[FC Nyva Bershad|Nyva Bershad]]. In 2010 was the club refounded."}}
